<p>Iran’s exiled former crown prince Reza Pahlavi was splashed with a red liquid as he left a news conference at Germany’s federal press conference building in Berlin on Thursday. Authorities said he appeared unhurt. Several reports said the substance appeared to be tomato sauce or tomato juice, and German police detained an alleged perpetrator shortly afterward. The incident came after Pahlavi used his Berlin appearance to criticize the ceasefire between the United States and Iran and urge European governments to do more to support the Iranian people. Video shared by multiple outlets showed him leaving with his security team, waving to supporters, and driving away after the splashing, suggesting the confrontation was brief and did not escalate further.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/pXJHDRzig_uGH3UT8gynfy6O5Js-i_lP05YvDJ-2iwpgBjWQl--r6zRO_a-GpzAmTYkbhgNSRxFHF3BMGEVXH88T1aoS4px3fjQ3RF0Z1xgUBFLKotBlfRaxAyNgcWIKueL9-bT2pqX448v4nOml1Txnbnn42vc4fB5Bd2MDgkKTTPt-cK3v' alt='Reza Pahlavi after being splashed with red liquid in Berlin.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Caught on camera: Video cited by broadcasters and newspapers showed a man with a backpack walking behind Pahlavi before throwing the red liquid as security closed in.</li><li>Police response: German police treated the incident as an attack and detained a suspect, described in some reports as a male alleged perpetrator.</li><li>Political setting: Pahlavi’s Berlin visit focused on calls for stronger European backing for Iranians, giving the protest that followed a clear political backdrop.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Reza Pahlavi: At his Berlin appearance, he urged European governments to do more to support the Iranian people. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/reza-pahlavi-splattered-with-red-liquid-in-berlin/article70897305.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>German police: Police treated the incident as an attack and moved to detain a suspect after the splashing. (<a href='htt